{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/974749-resonance-effects","id":974749,"title":"Resonance Effects","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-22T16:58:15-07:00","id":974749,"title":"Resonance Effects","content":"Would it be a good idea to mix concept of resonance in ascension and Branding backlash in dark ages?<br /> <br /> The two already pretty similar, though resonance has better defined effects and branding has a wider range of benefits and drawbacks(weird enough that a paradox backlash can have &quot;benefits&quot;). Resonance could be expanded so that it causes effects not only on the mages magic, but their mundane skills as well. A mage with 2 dots of entropic(terrifying) resonance could have a +2 added to the difficulty of intimidation/leadership rolls, but suffer a -2 to seduction/persuasion rolls. It could have physical effects as well, said mage could be becoming more wild and animistic looking as their resonance grew.<br /> <br /> The effects on magic could also be larger. Much like how higher resonance causes small effects without the mages input, having a mages magic influenced by resonance make it easier for the mage to get what the want, but have less control over How it's done. Like unleashing in dark ages fae, having resonance and magic working in concert could cause a mage simply trying to create food turn the area around him into a feast(the rocks suddenly shifting into bread, animals becoming fresh dishes, plants becoming bowls of vegetables, etc.). Effects could also similarly spin out of control, like having a mage role highest aligned resounance vs arete(if arete roll wins, effect continue like always. if resonance wins, the mage is in for a surprise).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactio